# Order 1769-9gna: the private PulseAudio server a browser window plays to.
# Operator ruling 2026-10-17: the browser sees only generic device names, never
# a host one; no host WirePlumber change, no renaming of host devices.
#
# chromium-framework-launch.sh starts this server inside the window's
# container and points the browser at it. Its ONLY device is one sink,
# "Speakers", a tunnel to the tray's output-only server (the socket file the
# window is given, see crates/tillandsias-headless/src/host_audio_pulse.conf),
# which plays to the host's default sink and refuses every record stream.
# So the browser can list exactly:
#   - Speakers             (the tunnel sink)
#   - Monitor of Speakers  (every PulseAudio sink has one; it carries only this
#                           window's own sound, and capture is denied anyway
#                           by the managed policy, 1767-5q4b)
# No device module, no network module, no other source. Clients of this
# server cannot load modules (the launcher passes --disallow-module-loading).
#
# @SOCKET@ (this server's socket) and @UPSTREAM@ (the output-only socket) are
# the only substitutions.
.fail
load-module module-native-protocol-unix socket=@SOCKET@ auth-anonymous=1
load-module module-tunnel-sink-new server=unix:@UPSTREAM@ sink_name=speakers sink_properties=device.description=Speakers
set-default-sink speakers
